                /** @description Soil-array serving mode. **false (default, combined):** each soil depth is served as ONE series — the mean of the probes that survived QC at that depth and timestamp, with `n_obs` reporting how many probes contributed. A depth backed by a single probe is therefore unchanged, and a depth whose probes disagree is served as their average rather than as one designated sensor. **true (split):** the per-probe series (`_a`, `_b`, … suffixes on the depth, e.g. `soil_vwc_0010_a`) are served IN ADDITION to the combined series — nothing is removed, so a consumer can compare the mean against its inputs in one response. Naming a probe explicitly (`elements=soil_vwc_0010_a`) returns it regardless of this flag, exactly as `elements=ppt_corrected` does in merged precipitation mode. The per-probe elements are `public=false`, so they are absent from the default `/elements/` listing — discover them with `/elements/?public=false`. **Provenance is mixed across the record:** before a station's probe-split date the depth has only one probe (the combined series IS that probe's series, and no `_a`/`_b` element exists for it), after it the depth has several; a window spanning that date carries both regimes. This parameter is independent of `level` — it selects which SERIES appear, while `level` selects how much QC has been applied to each. */
                split_arrays?: boolean;
                /** @description Precipitation serving mode. **false (default, merged):** `ppt` is the wind-corrected precipitation series — at level 2, gauge-vibration false accumulation recorded during high-wind events is replaced by the mass recovered from the Pluvio bucket weight. Inside such an event the per-timestamp value is null (unknown — not zero), and the event's recovered total appears as a single ACCUMULATED value on the row at the event's end; `/observations/flags/` explains every such row (ppt_event_unknown, ppt_event_accumulated, ppt_event_region, ppt_event_unrecovered — a no-anchor event's raw reading served unrecovered). In merged mode `ppt_corrected` never appears as a separate element at any level. **true (split):** the previous two-series behavior — raw-cleaned `ppt` plus the separate `ppt_corrected` element, at every level. Explicitly requesting `elements=ppt_corrected` returns the corrected series regardless of this flag. Levels 0 and 1 always serve unmerged `ppt` values. */
                split_ppt?: boolean;
                /** @description QC tier, identical on every endpoint. 0 = raw, exactly as reported by the station. 1 = provisional: cleaned by the row-local ingest checks only (hard range breaches nulled); values condemned by the daily batch checks (step, persistence, wind-affected precipitation, shared-sensor, accumulation ceiling) are retained. 2 (default) = operational: fully cleaned by all checks, and `ppt` is the wind-corrected precipitation series unless `split_ppt=true` (see that parameter). Where the daily QC pipeline has not yet processed a level-2 row, its provisional value is served and the `provisional` column is true; such rows firm up after the next morning's pipeline (QC batch 07:01, ppt recovery 07:30, finalize 08:00 America/Denver). */
                level?: number;
                /** @description The output format of data. Can be 'html', 'json', or 'csv'. */
                type?: components["schemas"]["Types"];
                /** @description Hourly/daily aggregates are always computed over the observations that exist — partial-coverage buckets are served, matching the legacy production API (request `na_info=true` for per-bucket completeness: `has_na` and `obs_count`). `rm_na` only affects long-format (`wide=false`) responses: with **rm_na=false** (the default), rows whose value is NULL are omitted; with **rm_na=true**, NULL-valued rows are included. */
                rm_na?: boolean;
                /** @description Whether to select only active stations, or both active and inactive stations. */
                active?: boolean;
                /** @description Whether or not to only select variables of interest to the general public. */
                public?: boolean;
                /** @description Whether to use wide or long format to view data */
                wide?: boolean;
                /** @description Units to display data in. Either 'US' for units used in U.S. or 'SI' for metric */
                units?: components["schemas"]["Units"];
                /** @description String of timezone to use for data aggregation. See valid options here: https://pvlib-python.readthedocs.io/en/stable/timetimezones.html */
                tz?: string;
                /** @description Whether to truncate seconds off of observation date time. */
                simple_datetime?: boolean;
                /** @description Station statistics to produce. List of options can be found at https://mesonet.climate.umt.edu/api/v2/elements. If left blank, all statistics will be returned. Additionally, a partial element match (e.g., `soil_vwc` or `air_temp`) can be used to get all elements of that type regardless of observation height/depth. */
                elements?: components["schemas"]["Elements"][] | null;
                /** @description Stations to collect data from. Can either be a single station (e.g. aceabsar) or a comma separated list of stations (e.g. aceabsar,arskeogh). If left blank, data from all stations will be returned. */
                stations?: components["schemas"]["Stations"][] | null;
